    {
      "id": "claim_7303ff42a4584793a9c37d24696bf16f",
      "statement": "Intent routing is a two-pass boundary: deterministic regex matching extracts start and embedded intents first, and an available LLM fallback is invoked only when regex finds none; malformed fallback data or subprocess errors leave the regex result intact.",
